# Arrays (Part 1)

Arrays are one of the most important data structures in programming.

An Array is a collection of elements of the same data type stored in contiguous memory locations.

Arrays help us store multiple values using a single variable name and form the foundation for many advanced Data Structures and Algorithms topics.

---

## Why Learn Arrays?

Arrays are used in:

- Data Structures & Algorithms (DSA)
- Competitive Programming
- Coding Interviews
- Searching Algorithms
- Sorting Algorithms
- Real-World Applications

Arrays are the foundation for:

- ArrayLists
- Strings
- Matrices (2D Arrays)
- Linked Lists
- Stacks
- Queues
- Trees
- Graphs

